cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Running Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on NVIDIA DGX Spark with PLE Disk Mmap and vLLM MTP"
message: "If you use this setup, benchmark wrappers, or PLE mmap architecture, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rawat"
    given-names: "Rajendra Singh"
    affiliation: "cogni.chat"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-5017-1341"
repository-code: "https://github.com/airawatraj/dgx-spark-qwen38-flash-agent"
abstract: >-
  A production-ready technical implementation and benchmarking suite for running
  RadixArk/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-NVFP4 (~176B total params, 6B active) on NVIDIA DGX Spark
  (GB10 Grace-Blackwell, 128 GB unified memory). By serving the 51B parameter n-gram PLE
  embedding table from NVMe disk via multithreaded mmap, resident GPU memory drops from
  122 GiB to ~76 GiB, freeing ~52 GiB of unified pool for KV cache (~720k–790k tokens).
  Includes native MTP speculative decoding, YaRN context extension up to 500K tokens,
  and native agentic tool calling.
keywords:
  - "Qwen3.8-Flash-Next"
  - "DGX Spark"
  - "GB10"
  - "Grace Blackwell"
  - "vLLM"
  - "PLE MMAP"
  - "Speculative Decoding"
  - "MTP"
  - "YaRN"
  - "AI Agents"
  - "NVFP4"
  - "Sparse Attention"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-28"
